{
  "decision_id": "DR-F2-0011-001",
  "kind": "data_layout",
  "question": "Copybook SQLCA (SYS-PORTFOLIO-001-FIL-0017) line 6 contains 'EXEC SQL INCLUDE SQLCA END-EXEC', naming itself. The included SQL communication area (SQLCODE, SQLSTATE, SQLERRMC, ...) has no layout in any reverse artifact. How should the forward design obtain the SQLCA layout and the SQLCODE/SQLSTATE semantics used by the 14 DB2 programs?",
  "options_recorded": [
    "Treat the include as the IBM DB2 precompiler-supplied SQLCA and supply its standard layout from authoritative IBM documentation as a documented external dependency (requires SME confirmation of the DB2 version).",
    "Do not model an SQLCA record; map SQLCODE/SQLSTATE checks to JDBC SQLException error code and SQLState in the Java design, with the SQL-STATUS-CODES constants as the SQLSTATE comparison table.",
    "Obtain the real SQLCA member from the source library (the repository copy appears to be a placeholder that shadows it) and re-run the reverse harness."
  ],
